 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation, and its repeats: Don Ottavio sings il zelo, il zelo del mio cor twice more than Donna Anna, and Donna Elvira repeats tradito, il mio and vendichi. The first sung syllable, -mor! (bar 1, Leporello), ends his prova farà d'amor! from the piece before (Presto, presto, pria ch'ei venga), so it is left out of the phrases here; Leporello sings nothing else in this piece, and his part is played but not offered as a role. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S29) and the IPA was checked against Castel. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
